From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nostalfinals <yuu8583@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 02:53:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Integrate Content System item boundaries

Route gameplay hooks through source-compatible enriched Item overloads while preserving vanilla subclass dispatch and exact crafting, combat, destruction, and container-fit call sites. Keep active-use side effects and kinetic precedence in ItemStack, and recover creative stacks before validation.

Encode ItemStack and ItemStackTemplate persistence through the Content System persistent form, recover after decode, recursively carry nested envelopes, and project every network stack for its receiving viewer. Make container remote slots retain canonical and projected snapshots with revision-aware claims, and use the same projected values for initial, slot, cursor, inventory, equipment, and entity-data packets.

Freeze the data component type registry before item compose handlers run so item builders can resolve bound vanilla and custom component holders. This changes only bootstrap freeze ordering and adds no steady-state allocation or runtime cost.

Projection work remains synchronous and allocates viewer-specific packet/state copies only when a stack or nested template crosses a boundary; unchanged remote runtime and revision skip modifier execution. The per-slot snapshots and opaque envelopes add bounded transient memory and metadata, while the centralized stream boundary, explicit registry dependency, and nested mapping add maintenance points when Mojang introduces new ItemStack-bearing components.

